The Core Commercial segment, anchored by [[Okami Central Station]] and the surrounding administrative districts, accounts for approximately 51% of total daily ridership. This concentration reflects the line's role as the primary feeder for the [[Harujima Shinkansen]] network and the numerous government ministries concentrated in the Otemachi area.

Peak-hour ridership is characterized by extreme directional imbalance. Morning rush hours (7:00–9:00 AM) see heavy southbound traffic as commuters from the northern residential suburbs of Yuyama and Tobe converge on the central business district. Evening rush hours (5:00–7:00 PM) reverse this pattern, with the northern platforms at Okami Central experiencing platform crowding indices exceeding 180% during the most congested 15-minute intervals.

==Rolling Stock==

The Miyoshi Line utilizes a specialized fleet of high-capacity commuter trains to handle its extreme ridership. All trains are 10-car sets, the longest in the metro system.

[[File:OkamiMetro_2000Series.jpg|thumb|left|220px|The veteran 2000 series at Rokumanji Station.]]

===2000 Series===
The 2000 series was the workhorse of the 1980s and 90s. These refurbished 10-car sets feature lavender exterior striping and were the first in Okaiken to introduce automated station announcements. They are constructed of unpainted stainless steel to reduce maintenance costs in the humid coastal environment of Suminoe. Despite their age, they remain popular for their spacious transverse seating in the end cars.

===30000 Series===
Introduced in 2011 to replace the original 1960s-era stock, these trains feature energy-efficient [[w:Variable-frequency drive|VVVF]] inverters and improved climate control. The interior features wood-grain panels as a tribute to the original 1935 Art Deco station designs. They are equipped with full-color LCD displays above every door, providing real-time transfer information and news updates.

[[File:OkamiMetro_4000Series_Interior.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Interior of the 4000 series showing the digital information displays.]]

===4000 Series===
The newest addition to the fleet, launched in 2023. These trains feature a Lavender-Modern aesthetic, wider passenger doors to speed up boarding at busy hubs like Okami Central, and onboard digital signage in four languages. They utilize advanced SiC (Silicon Carbide) power modules, making them 30% more energy-efficient than the 30000 series. They are being phased in as the primary stock for the Okami World Expo 2030, featuring onboard Wi-Fi and universal design spaces in every car.

